comment_data.body:
Thinking about this now, it's wrong to just calculate 10% out of `term->sb_size` as it now includes the 10% delta.
Since I'll need to know the delta that was appended to `term->sb_size` when calculating how many rows can be deleted, I was thinking of either declaring `static const int SCBK_DELTA = 1.1` and then taking it into account when calculating `sb_delete`. Another option I've thought of is to exit the loop that executes `ml_delete` when `buf->b_ml.ml_line_count - height <= term->sb_size`

@justinmk @bfredl WDYT?

